<!-- Creates the main container and adds spacing above the Projects page content. -->
<div class="container mt-3">

  <!-- Creates a centred Bootstrap card with a light grey background and maximum width of 800px. -->
  <div class="card mx-auto mb-3 bg-light" style="max-width: 800px;">

    <div class="card-body">

      <!-- Displays the page title passed from the Express route. -->
      <h1 class="card-title"><%= title %></h1>

      <!-- Introduces the academic and technical projects featured on this page. -->
      <p class="lead">
        This page showcases some of the academic and technical projects
        I have completed throughout my studies at Ontario Tech University.
      </p>

      <!-- Main heading for the projects section. -->
      <h2 class="mb-3">My Projects</h2>

      <!-- First project: Network simulation completed using Cisco Packet Tracer. -->
      <h3>Cisco Packet Tracer - Intro to Networking II</h3>
      <p>
        Completed a network simulation involving multiple sites, routers,
        switches, VLANs, IP addresses, interfaces, and routing configurations.
        The project also included connecting sites such as Ontario Tech
        Residence, Toronto, Chicago, and Mexico, along with DNS and web servers.
      </p>

      <!-- Second project: Python banking simulator developed as a group project. -->
      <h3>Banking System Simulator - Object-Oriented Programming</h3>
      <p>
        Developed a banking system simulator in Python as part of a group
        project. The program allowed users to create customers and accounts,
        make deposits and withdrawals, transfer funds, apply interest,
        manage transactions, and save or load system data using JSON.
      </p>

      <!-- Third project: Group analysis of leadership styles presented in a video. -->
      <h3>Leadership Analysis Video - Collaborative Leadership</h3>
      <p>
        Worked with a group to analyze Darth Vader's leadership style using
        concepts and terminology from the course. We examined how leadership
        techniques such as control and punishment were used and presented
        our analysis in a video.
      </p>

      <!-- Fourth project: Computer architecture calculations and concepts. -->
      <h3>Assignment 1 - Computer Architecture</h3>
      <p>
        Completed a series of computer architecture calculations involving
        clock rates, CPU performance, CPI, CPU time, and comparisons between
        computer systems. The assignment also covered cache concepts such
        as byte offsets, cache line indexes, and memory blocks.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
